      "value": "@{69bed226bcda4ee63244d35d|full_name} someone gave me a month of VRC+ recently and I took the opportunity to age verify. I think there are two different problems vrchat needs to address. \n\nThe first, as things are right now, a user only needs to have a VRC+ on the day they wish to do the age verification procedure, and they haven't done a good job of messaging that. Some amount of users would be okay with a one time $10 Yankee dollar expense. Maybe they need to make it easier to only \"Subscribe\" for a single month. Subscribing off of a steam wallet balance and just don't have the money for the second month would be one work around.\n\nThe second group to address is getting that age verification price down as low as possible. Vrchat hasn't gotten that done yet, so I'm personally curious about what other people think. Like would you age verify if the cost was a one time cost 2/3 of what vrchat plus would cost? I guess \"2/3\" is a crap way to say a fraction. I asked the other person about half or two thirds, I'm just going to ask about half.\n\nWith your situation in mind, Would you spring for a one time cost of $5 USD?\n\nMaybe they could do a lottery of X free age verifications every month (someone suggested this recently on here), but I know they can't just give it away to everyone on demand. Just as an example say it costs vrchat a US dollar for one account to be age verified. How many people could you pay 1-20  cents to create an age verified account? I saw someone suggest that sort of financial amplification attack on the forums months ago so the idea isn't new.\n\nI just re read my older comment here, and yeah, I totally forgot about the bread.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
